  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Belongs as a member of INV-numat — the umbrella covers vocabulary fields whose values mix axes from distinct conceptual dimensions, and `modifiers` exhibits the same per-emitter-dialect pattern that umbrella catalogues for framework_dispatch and call_construct. Sibling to WI-moliz (extends/inherits/implements divergence on edge.type — same cross-language vocabulary asymmetry on a different field). Distinct from the umbrella's existing members in that `modifiers` is `List[str]` not scalar — current axis-declaration check at multi_value_field_axis.py only covers scalar `str` / `Optional[str]` / `Literal`. Fixing this also requires extending the axis-declaration policy in ADR-0024 to cover list-valued and dict-valued vocabulary fields. Related to INV-zigup (cross_language meta same writer-side root cause: per-linker code paths with no shared emission policy)."  # dcc0
